\section{Introduction}
Schlieren imaging provides a direct visualization of refractive index gradients
arising from density variations in compressible flows. In this work, we elevate
Schlieren physics into a deterministic cryptographic engine. The refractive
index is governed by the Gladstone--Dale relation
\begin{equation}
    n(\mathbf{r},t) = 1 + K\rho(\mathbf{r},t),
\end{equation}
where $\rho$ is the density field and $K$ a refractivity constant.

